ROUTER VS SWITCH COMPARISON
===========================

+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------+
| FEATURE           | ROUTER                      | SWITCH                      |
+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------+
| Main Use          | Connects different networks | Connects devices in a LAN   |
| Typical Location  | Home, office, ISP edge      | Office, lab, server room    |
| Data Handling     | Uses IP addresses           | Uses MAC addresses          |
| Network Layer     | Layer 3                     | Layer 2                     |
| Internet          | Connects LAN to internet    | Connects devices in LAN     |
| Example           | Home internet router        | College network switch      |
| Ports             | WAN and LAN ports           | Multiple Ethernet ports     |
+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------+

KEY DIFFERENCE:
Router = Connects different networks
Switch = Connects devices within the same network
